MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello all,

The latest version of poppr, 2.7 has been released on CRAN with binaries for macOS and Windows. This release gives two new functions and an algorithmic change. Details can be found here: https://github.com/grunwaldlab/poppr/releases/tag/v.2.7.0

Function make_haplotypes() will split your higher ploidy data into pseudo-haplotypes. This was a previously internal function for poppr.amova().

Function as.genambig() will convert your genind/genclone data to polysat's genambig class.

The results of poppr.amova() when within = FALSE will change due to an oversight causing the distance calculated to be dissimilarity instead of Euclidean. Thanks goes to Patrick Meirmans for pointing this out and providing test code for polyploid AMOVA.

